KZ2 patch 6078 (diagnostic): LD_VC_NEW=1, which draws the payload cache misses and why.

An earlier change measured ~350 new fetch keys per frame in b-walk's heavy views (refs+remap+fetch ~3 ms/f there) and
guessed dynamic geometry at new ring offsets. Before converting anything once per buffer write instead of once per
draw, this counts, per missed draw after its fetch: the reason (first sight of the key, second sight = fill,
invalidated, dynamic, main memory without LD_VTX_CACHE_MAIN, ineligible key); its source spans as patch 2047 takes
them (index range, each used attribute's element range), whether any is in main memory, whether one had a tracked
write this frame (fresh), in the last two frames (fresh2) or neither (stale); whether the draw's whole source
signature, and each attribute span (location, offset, length, type, size, stride), was already converted this frame
by another draw (repeat: the work a per-buffer conversion would save, weighted by vertices) or last frame (prev:
stable data under a key that changed for another reason); and the six 1 MB regions with the most missed vertices.
[vc-new] per 256 frames with RSX_PERF. Observes only; off by default.

